{
  "title": "medieval_castle.jpg",
  "intro": {
    "_doc": "The title's fly-in (0.00307, ui/titleIntro.js; a prototype): file = the clip in assets/video/, a flight from far across the valley into the title painting, its last frame the painting itself cover-fit with the game's vignette baked over the whole film (0.00310), so the held frame fades onto the 3D renderer's rest pose with no jump (docs/video-prompts.md says how it is made; a new clip is a new filename, rule 7). enabled false = no intro. waitMs = how long the loader waits at 100% for the clip before the title shows without it; leadMs = the fade begins this long BEFORE the film's end, the film still playing under it (0.00308, the developer's ask: a crossfade a little earlier); holdMs = with leadMs 0, the last frame held after the end before the fade; fadeMs = the fade onto the painting; whooshDb = its trim under the game's level (-1.9 dB = 20% quieter, 0.00310, the developer's ask); whooshAtMs = where in the flight a room change's whoosh peaks (0.00309, the developer's ask; the Descend strike sounds as the title's panel comes up — both only where the browser let the title bed start before a gesture, or after the phone's PLAY tap). Played once per session; a click, a tap or a key skips it; reduced motion and a browser without H.264 skip it.",
    "enabled": true,
    "file": "title_flyin_v2.mp4",
    "waitMs": 1500,
    "holdMs": 0,
    "leadMs": 300,
    "fadeMs": 700,
    "whooshAtMs": 1700,
