  "parallax": {
    "_doc": "3D backgrounds (0.083, core/bg3d.js): depth maps in assets/bg/depth/ (tools/gen-depth.py). depthScale = how far depth pushes the art along each camera ray; pivot = the depth that stays still; yaw/pitch = sway amplitude in degrees; periods in seconds; overscan = skirt beyond the screen edge; overrides = per-file tweaks keyed by background filename. joltDeg = the small camera kick on heavy blows; swayDeg = the rocking rotation (about the depth centre) on the biggest blows (0.092/0.093; crits, SMASH, multi-kills swing the near art right, hits on the knight of at least swayHitShare of max HP swing it left). depthFiles = per-background depth map filename when regenerated (new name, never overwrite). fog (0.099; puffs 0.101, core/bg3dPuffs.js) = depth-embedded mist: distance haze + large soft mist puffs drifting through the scene volume; amount per background in overrides (long exterior views more, rooms a touch), colour from the scene's own far pixels (fogColor [r,g,b] 0-1 overrides it). 0.167: toned down to the developer's reference (drift spread 0.7-1.0, turbulence 0.015 / 12 s, breathe 0.04, bob 0.006, pulse 0.3; winds x0.7). 0.166: every painting has its own fog and fogWind (outdoors and the large halls a notch windier); the base is the Fog Lab's Rolling Mist with the developer's drift 3.5, haze 0.38 / curve 1.55. fogWind = drift in world units/s [sideways +right, up, toward the camera +] per background; fogSpeed multiplies it. puffs = count, size range, height range (y), box half-width, near/far distance (the art spans ~0.6-1.4; the focal plane is 1) with fading bands, soft = how gently a puff fades into the scene in front of it, opacity. 0.164 (the Fog Lab, labs/fog/ since 0.168): drift = per-puff wind speed spread, rock = rocking amplitude range (rad), period = the rock/breathe cycle range (s), bob = vertical bob (world units), breathe = size pulse share, shadeVar / alphaVar = per-puff brightness and opacity spread, turbulence = how far each puff wanders on its own (world units) over turbulencePeriod s, pulse = how much each puff fades in and out over pulsePeriod s, flow = how fast the mist churns inside each puff (noise uv/s) at flowScale, thinning by flowAmount. mist = the puffs' lighting: shade = how strong the baked self-shadow reads, litTint / shadeTint = colour multipliers for the lit and shaded sides, sceneLight = how much the painting's own bright pixels (torches, windows) light the mist, nearBright = extra brightness for near puffs. haze = the distance haze on the art: density, curve (power on the far share), high = how much survives high up, strength, max. maxPixels = canvas pixel budget; minFps = below this the quality steps down (lower resolution, then no fog, then flat). lights (0.100, core/bg3dLights.js) = the flash a crit / potion / revive puts into the scene in front of the character: dist = how far in front of the camera (focal plane 1), radius = reach in world units, per kind colour, strength, fade and life in seconds; enabled false switches them off. push (0.171, the room transition): the camera dollies dist world units into the painting (the focal plane is 1 away) from the moment the windows start to fade, over inMs (accelerating); the next painting appears pushed in and pulls back to rest over outMs (decelerating) through the crossfade and the windows' return — one movement through the picture. Tune it in the Fog Lab (the arrows play the real sequence). 0.00197: motionMaxFps = the frame-rate cap while a jolt, sway, flash or push plays (maxFps holds when nothing moves; it used to be uncapped then, i.e. 144 fps on a 144 Hz screen through most of a fight); quality = the ladder's sensitivity: the frame rate is measured over windowMs, a gap over gapMs between frames is a pause (hidden tab) and resets the window, slowWindows slow windows in a row step down one rung (and a window is slow only against the rate the maxFps throttle can reach on this screen, so a 40 Hz display is not punished); lights.rise = the flash's rise time in seconds. 0.00222: phone = the phone power profile (shared/platform.js isPhone, the device — a tablet keeps the desktop values; ?desktop skips it): the knobs that differ on a phone, merged over the base by bgTuning.js tuning() before the per-file overrides — maxDpr 1.5 (1278 px wide on an 852-px phone: 44% fewer fragments than DPR 2), maxFps 24 at rest, motionMaxFps 30, puffDiv 3; puffDiv = the mist buffer's divisor (the puffs are drawn at 1/puffDiv of the canvas and composited over it; 2 was a constant in the renderer); quality.reachShare = the share of the throttle's reachable rate a window must draw (0.9 in src since 0.00197 — and applied to a struggling device's own rate too, so nobody ever stepped down: the ladder judges against minFps once the rAF rate is at or under maxFps).",
